## Terms and Conditions

### 1. Definitions
- **"Software"** means the DPUF binary format specification, reference encoders, C AVX2 Zero-Decode runtime engine, living container profiler, and all associated code in this repository.
- **"Commercial Use"** means any use, deployment, or integration of the Software for direct or indirect commercial advantage, monetary compensation, revenue generation, or incorporation into commercial software, SaaS platforms, or proprietary internal enterprise workloads.
- **"Platform Embedding"** means integrating, packaging, wrapping, or redistributing the Software, format decoder, or kernels as a component of a multi-model serving platform, local AI manager, or developer tool distributed to third parties.

### 2. Permitted Free Uses (No License Fee)
Subject to Section 4 (Attribution and Notice):
- **Academic & Scientific Research:** You may freely inspect, modify, evaluate, and publish academic research utilizing DPUF at any scale without charge.
- **Personal & Local Development:** Individual developers, students, and hobbyists may freely build, test, and run models locally for non-commercial personal projects.
- **Open-Source Non-Commercial Tooling:** Purely open-source tools with no commercial monetization, paid tiers, or outside venture funding may interface with DPUF.

### 3. Commercial & Enterprise Licensing Requirement
If you intend to use, integrate, or redistribute the Software for:
- Production deployment within a commercial business, enterprise, or government entity;
- Providing a paid API, cloud inference service, or hosted LLM backend;
- Embedding DPUF support within a commercial software application, developer platform, or multi-model management runner;
- Closed-source redistribution;

You **do not** receive a grant under Section 2. You must contact **D. P. (dule_pan)** to purchase and execute a valid **DPUF Enterprise Commercial License Agreement**.

